(2367804, 328006, 51638, '<td valign="top">Maybe selective desat might have worked better here than a straight b/w? Just a thought. Nice DOF though.</td>', 'Maybe selective desat might have worked better here than a straight b/w? Just a thought. Nice DOF though.', '2006-05-01 10:06:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(2367807, 327821, 49930, '<td valign="top">Lovely framing. You have filled the frame with the pattern. It draws the eye in. Well done.</td>', 'Lovely framing. You have filled the frame with the pattern. It draws the eye in. Well done.', '2006-05-01 10:07:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(2367808, 328411, 30049, '<td valign="top">This is an enjoyable image, and I really like the concept that is being envisioned here.  Potential here is very high.  What pulls it down for me is the stairs to the left.  Try cropping this by bringing the bottom up to remove the seam where the column meets the sidewalk and trim off the left side to remove the stairs.  How is it?  Probably would need to reshoot and position yourself a little differently to compose it more to the right.  JMO.  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'This is an enjoyable image, and I really like the concept that is being envisioned here.  Potential here is very high.  What pulls it down for me is the stairs to the left.  Try cropping this by bringing the bottom up to remove the seam where the column meets the sidewalk and trim off the left side to remove the stairs.  How is it?  Probably would need to reshoot and position yourself a little differently to compose it more to the right.  JMO.  Good luck in the challenge.', '2006-05-01 10:08:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(2367818, 328265, 30049, '<td valign="top">Something in the color seems off...too yellow maybe?  A bit tight on the composition.  Need more space past the dogs, especially the dog on the left.  While this is a cute pic, the viewer is torn in which way to look.  Generally, negative space is left in the direction the subject is looking.  Here, in both cases the viewer is taken directly out of the frame on either side.  JMO.  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Something in the color seems off...too yellow maybe?  A bit tight on the composition.  Need more space past the dogs, especially the dog on the left.  While this is a cute pic, the viewer is torn in which way to look.  Generally, negative space is left in the direction the subject is looking.  Here, in both cases the viewer is taken directly out of the frame on either side.  JMO.  Good luck in the challenge.', '2006-05-01 10:12:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(2367819, 328404, 5792, '<td valign="top">Simplicity is good. You might consider cloning out the the branch at center bottom.</td>', 'Simplicity is good. You might consider cloning out the the branch at center bottom.', '2006-05-01 10:12:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(2367822, 328321, 5792, '<td valign="top">Pretty model, nice pose, yellowish color cast.</td>', 'Pretty model, nice pose, yellowish color cast.', '2006-05-01 10:13:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(2367827, 328335, 30049, '<td valign="top">The black on the dogs muzzle/jaw area looks washed out, like this was underexposed and brought up in PP to lighten it some?  Not sure why, but the dog looks very isolated/disconnected from the background, especially near the lower jaw and grass.</td>', 'The black on the dogs muzzle/jaw area looks washed out, like this was underexposed and brought up in PP to lighten it some?  Not sure why, but the dog looks very isolated/disconnected from the background, especially near the lower jaw and grass.', '2006-05-01 10:14:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(2367846, 327842, 51638, '<td valign="top">I like the strong diagonal created by the ''soft'' water and the difference in colouration and exposure on either side of it. Well done.</td>', 'I like the strong diagonal created by the ''soft'' water and the difference in colouration and exposure on either side of it. Well done.', '2006-05-01 10:20:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(2367853, 328322, 5792, '<td valign="top">Beautiful waterfall. You might consider a much smaller crop to eliminates the out of focus foreground water.</td>', 'Beautiful waterfall. You might consider a much smaller crop to eliminates the out of focus foreground water.', '2006-05-01 10:22:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(2367860, 327915, 51638, '<td valign="top">Very cool. I wish I was as good with PP.</td>', 'Very cool. I wish I was as good with PP.', '2006-05-01 10:23:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(2367867, 327895, 5792, '<td valign="top">Tender capture. There appears to be a red color cast that shows up in skin tones. A simple solution for that is to add Hue/Saturation adjustment layer and simply reducing the saturation of red. I think you will find the improvement in skin tones to be surprisingly dramatic.</td>', 'Tender capture. There appears to be a red color cast that shows up in skin tones. A simple solution for that is to add Hue/Saturation adjustment layer and simply reducing the saturation of red. I think you will find the improvement in skin tones to be surprisingly dramatic.', '2006-05-01 10:25:19.000000', NULL, 1),
