(2389947, 327720, 16488, '<td valign="top">I so want to say "good catch!" and not have you take it the wrong way....<br/> <br/>Love the moment and the "story" in this image. The composition, texture of the footprints, pattern placement...nicely done!</td>', 'I so want to say "good catch!" and not have you take it the wrong way.... Love the moment and the "story" in this image. The composition, texture of the footprints, pattern placement...nicely done!', '2006-05-07 13:34:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(2389957, 328537, 16488, '<td valign="top">So other-worldly! Wonderful forms in the fore-ground! Unearthly green rope and sand! Nice capture of the moon, stars and jet! Wide angle really accentuates the swing of rope and curve of the earth. Minor distraction with the water under the rope on the left...would have cloned over it with beach or cropped the image in from the left to keep the eye from escaping the frame. I really like this though---so pleasantly weird!</td>', 'So other-worldly! Wonderful forms in the fore-ground! Unearthly green rope and sand! Nice capture of the moon, stars and jet! Wide angle really accentuates the swing of rope and curve of the earth. Minor distraction with the water under the rope on the left...would have cloned over it with beach or cropped the image in from the left to keep the eye from escaping the frame. I really like this though---so pleasantly weird!', '2006-05-07 13:38:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(2389959, 327891, 16488, '<td valign="top">Interesting study...looking forard to the notes.</td>', 'Interesting study...looking forard to the notes.', '2006-05-07 13:39:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(2389960, 327774, 16488, '<td valign="top">I like the expression and the lighting from a single source. The division of the face down the median adds interest, though I wish the head were tipped a bit more to the model''s left to take advantage of the potential for a partial profile there. The hand gesture is difficult to read in the image--yes, pensive and a bit of a press against the lips--but an odd thing is happening with the lower finger. The position and blending of the second finger with the face makes it begin to look like the lower jaw...once that idea occurred to me, I found it almost impossible to shake the strange concept....</td>', 'I like the expression and the lighting from a single source. The division of the face down the median adds interest, though I wish the head were tipped a bit more to the model''s left to take advantage of the potential for a partial profile there. The hand gesture is difficult to read in the image--yes, pensive and a bit of a press against the lips--but an odd thing is happening with the lower finger. The position and blending of the second finger with the face makes it begin to look like the lower jaw...once that idea occurred to me, I found it almost impossible to shake the strange concept....', '2006-05-07 13:39:06.000000', NULL, 1),
