(2394762, 327848, 31794, '<td valign="top">[[trading post]]<br/> <br/>even though there are some lovely colors in this image there is no main subject to focus on, the eye keeps wandering all over the image looking for the subject, but it''s not there...<br/> <br/>in this image a small girl, maby 5 years old in a summer dress walking the road would make this a perfect image.. I know the 5year olds are hard to get if you didn''t make one in time ;) but this is just the perfect scene for a picture like that.<br/> <br/>without the main subject this picure is average at the most..<br/> <br/>just my 2¢</td>', '[[trading post]] even though there are some lovely colors in this image there is no main subject to focus on, the eye keeps wandering all over the image looking for the subject, but it''s not there... in this image a small girl, maby 5 years old in a summer dress walking the road would make this a perfect image.. I know the 5year olds are hard to get if you didn''t make one in time ;) but this is just the perfect scene for a picture like that. without the main subject this picure is average at the most.. just my 2¢', '2006-05-08 20:15:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(2394782, 327615, 36371, '<td valign="top">Hmm. and all at the expense of ''''the four you see which were killed and mounted onto the flower".<br/>So let me get this straight...you win a blue ribbon by using dead bugs (that you killed) and are quite insensitive about it, I might add, and you create an unrealistic image and add a nice title to it...is that how it''s done?<br/>As this photo has that ''''WOW'''' factor, I don''t think any of us will ever see this replicated in real life. I have real mixed feelings about this one. <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-05-08 19:59:34.</i></td>', 'Hmm. and all at the expense of ''''the four you see which were killed and mounted onto the flower".So let me get this straight...you win a blue ribbon by using dead bugs (that you killed) and are quite insensitive about it, I might add, and you create an unrealistic image and add a nice title to it...is that how it''s done?As this photo has that ''''WOW'''' factor, I don''t think any of us will ever see this replicated in real life. I have real mixed feelings about this one. ', '2006-05-08 20:22:13.000000', '2006-05-08 20:59:34.000000', 0),
(2394800, 328534, 31794, '<td valign="top">[[trading post]]<br/> <br/>even though this image is ok it makes a really bad choice for free study, this is the challenge where people are voted down for lack of creativity, and this image lacks all creativity, like a catalog picture.<br/> <br/>and the dark edges probably from the high pass filter makes it even worse.. <br/> <br/>airplanes can be good subjects, but they look better from below or from same level, they usually look uninteresting from above, just like your image.<br/> <br/>I''m not trying to be judgemental, but this image would have scored much higher in B/W challenge.<br/> <br/>just my 2¢</td>', '[[trading post]] even though this image is ok it makes a really bad choice for free study, this is the challenge where people are voted down for lack of creativity, and this image lacks all creativity, like a catalog picture. and the dark edges probably from the high pass filter makes it even worse..  airplanes can be good subjects, but they look better from below or from same level, they usually look uninteresting from above, just like your image. I''m not trying to be judgemental, but this image would have scored much higher in B/W challenge. just my 2¢', '2006-05-08 20:28:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2394857, 327615, 49497, '<td valign="top">Except the four?</td>', 'Except the four?', '2006-05-08 20:51:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(2394864, 328147, 32997, '<td valign="top">I don''t understand at all why a tail sticking out of the frame detracts from some people''s perception of what makes this work..i like it..there is something natural about having this..adds to the movement of the shot..<br/>nice work...</td>', 'I don''t understand at all why a tail sticking out of the frame detracts from some people''s perception of what makes this work..i like it..there is something natural about having this..adds to the movement of the shot..nice work...', '2006-05-08 20:53:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2394869, 327615, 3306, '<td valign="top">Glued Ladybugs, how could you do such a thing. I would never do anything like that. (Just Kidding!!) Congrats on a great image.</td>', 'Glued Ladybugs, how could you do such a thing. I would never do anything like that. (Just Kidding!!) Congrats on a great image.', '2006-05-08 20:55:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2394925, 327788, 20941, '<td valign="top">Wow! Congratulations on this Great Shot and a Personal Best!!</td>', 'Wow! Congratulations on this Great Shot and a Personal Best!!', '2006-05-08 21:17:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2394955, 327848, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment<br/>I liked this one when viewing the entries for this challenge.  The curved line of the road and the contrast of the pink on the green gives it a serene feeling, in my opinion.  It does need a bit more sharpness I think, to truly bring out the detail in the foliage.  This is one of those that I think is probably hurt by the limited size we have here - I''ll bet it''s lovely full size and it would probably make a very nice print.</td>', 'Trading Post commentI liked this one when viewing the entries for this challenge.  The curved line of the road and the contrast of the pink on the green gives it a serene feeling, in my opinion.  It does need a bit more sharpness I think, to truly bring out the detail in the foliage.  This is one of those that I think is probably hurt by the limited size we have here - I''ll bet it''s lovely full size and it would probably make a very nice print.', '2006-05-08 21:29:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2394976, 328534, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment<br/>While it''s only an "average" subject, the lighting here is great!  You''ve done an excellent job lighting the subject, maintaining excellent detail which is even more impressive given the object is black and chrome, and even creating a "texture" to the light beneath the subject.  I suspect the not-so-great score is based on limited appeal of the subject matter.  What you''ve done with the lighting, though, can be transferred to lots of other shots, and that''s a very good thing!</td>', 'Trading Post commentWhile it''s only an "average" subject, the lighting here is great!  You''ve done an excellent job lighting the subject, maintaining excellent detail which is even more impressive given the object is black and chrome, and even creating a "texture" to the light beneath the subject.  I suspect the not-so-great score is based on limited appeal of the subject matter.  What you''ve done with the lighting, though, can be transferred to lots of other shots, and that''s a very good thing!', '2006-05-08 21:38:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2394998, 327849, 42125, '<td valign="top">Comment from a member of your own commenting club :-)<br/>This is a picture showing a stone in front of a hill far away.<br/>Although it is a beautiful stone it is not something that makes you want to see it again. Maybe an animal or a person in front of it or on top of it would make a big different.<br/>What is good?:<br/>1. Good use of rule of thirds.<br/>2. Leading lines make you look at all the picture.<br/>3. Colours are good.<br/>4. Focus is good.<br/>5. Frame colour/darkness fits the picture well.<br/>What could be better?:<br/>1. The sky, like in many of my own pictures is blown, probably not because of wrong adjustments but just because it is like that when you take the picture.<br/>2. Wait for a better day to take pictures :-)<br/>Hope this helps!<br/>Edited: Deleted an empty line<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-05-10 20:26:47.</i></td>', 'Comment from a member of your own commenting club :-)This is a picture showing a stone in front of a hill far away.Although it is a beautiful stone it is not something that makes you want to see it again. Maybe an animal or a person in front of it or on top of it would make a big different.What is good?:1. Good use of rule of thirds.2. Leading lines make you look at all the picture.3. Colours are good.4. Focus is good.5. Frame colour/darkness fits the picture well.What could be better?:1. The sky, like in many of my own pictures is blown, probably not because of wrong adjustments but just because it is like that when you take the picture.2. Wait for a better day to take pictures :-)Hope this helps!Edited: Deleted an empty line', '2006-05-08 21:46:11.000000', '2006-05-10 21:26:47.000000', 0),
(2395032, 327761, 30982, '<td valign="top">Trading Post comment<br/>I''m not all that fond of the perspective though it does emphasize the point you make with the title.  I think the overall tone of the shot could be helped a bit by de-brightening it, either through curves or maybe contrast?  It does make you smile, though!</td>', 'Trading Post commentI''m not all that fond of the perspective though it does emphasize the point you make with the title.  I think the overall tone of the shot could be helped a bit by de-brightening it, either through curves or maybe contrast?  It does make you smile, though!', '2006-05-08 21:55:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2395047, 327615, 40667, '<td valign="top">Great Job! Really an amazing image, soo deserving of the blue! yah did a great job on this one, way 2 go!</td>', 'Great Job! Really an amazing image, soo deserving of the blue! yah did a great job on this one, way 2 go!', '2006-05-08 22:01:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(2395065, 327915, 55642, '<td valign="top">The girl is gorgeous, with nice color and clarity. I especially like the definition around her shoulder. I scored this at a 7 in voting. <br/> <br/>I think this photo probably suffered in several areas. First, from the dead space on the right. Second, she is obscuring the drummer behind her too much - seeing him in the background, even blurred, would have been cleaner and more interesting. There is also the assumption that a photojournalist wouldn''t normally selectively desaturate nearly the entire photo (in addition to whatever other process was used to almost plasticize them), though I''m guessing this was done to visually separate the girl from the drummer. Finally, the shadow cast by her arm is a little distracting, though this would be a difficult variable to control in this particular setting.</td>', 'The girl is gorgeous, with nice color and clarity. I especially like the definition around her shoulder. I scored this at a 7 in voting.  I think this photo probably suffered in several areas. First, from the dead space on the right. Second, she is obscuring the drummer behind her too much - seeing him in the background, even blurred, would have been cleaner and more interesting. There is also the assumption that a photojournalist wouldn''t normally selectively desaturate nearly the entire photo (in addition to whatever other process was used to almost plasticize them), though I''m guessing this was done to visually separate the girl from the drummer. Finally, the shadow cast by her arm is a little distracting, though this would be a difficult variable to control in this particular setting.', '2006-05-08 22:08:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2395098, 328451, 22099, '<td valign="top">Nice capture. You might try the same shot at 200 or even 400 ISO at the 30 sec. Your exposure would show even more detail of the Big Bipper as well as the area around it.</td>', 'Nice capture. You might try the same shot at 200 or even 400 ISO at the 30 sec. Your exposure would show even more detail of the Big Bipper as well as the area around it.', '2006-05-08 22:25:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2395101, 328232, 40718, '<td valign="top">I thought this was not bad.  I gave it a 5.  The problem I see is that it wants to be an abstract, but it isn''t quite abstract enough.  On the other hand, it wants to be a nature shot, but it''s too abstract.<br/> <br/>I wished you could have waited a split second so we could have had more of the ant visible.  Other than that, the composition is nice.  Both subjects are off center and balance each other.  The colors are nice as well.</td>', 'I thought this was not bad.  I gave it a 5.  The problem I see is that it wants to be an abstract, but it isn''t quite abstract enough.  On the other hand, it wants to be a nature shot, but it''s too abstract. I wished you could have waited a split second so we could have had more of the ant visible.  Other than that, the composition is nice.  Both subjects are off center and balance each other.  The colors are nice as well.', '2006-05-08 22:27:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2395112, 327750, 40718, '<td valign="top">I like frogs too Matt, but I gave this a 4.  Three issues, were they fixed, would have easily bumped this into the 6-7 range.<br/> <br/>1) Too centered.  Perhaps this is a result of being so zoomed.  I used to love to zoom into things. I''m learning that a bit more environment makes for a good picture.<br/> <br/>2) Motion blur.  I''m guessing the froggie didn''t let you use a tripod.  IS or not, 1/6 is pretty darn slow.  I noticed the blur right away and personally I tend to vote blurred or OOF shots fairly low.  Big sin on DPC.<br/> <br/>3) The highlight is quite harsh.  I''m not quite sure what to recommend.  A polarizer would have helped, but requires time to adjust as well as making the shutter even slower.  Was it your flash?</td>', 'I like frogs too Matt, but I gave this a 4.  Three issues, were they fixed, would have easily bumped this into the 6-7 range. 1) Too centered.  Perhaps this is a result of being so zoomed.  I used to love to zoom into things. I''m learning that a bit more environment makes for a good picture. 2) Motion blur.  I''m guessing the froggie didn''t let you use a tripod.  IS or not, 1/6 is pretty darn slow.  I noticed the blur right away and personally I tend to vote blurred or OOF shots fairly low.  Big sin on DPC. 3) The highlight is quite harsh.  I''m not quite sure what to recommend.  A polarizer would have helped, but requires time to adjust as well as making the shutter even slower.  Was it your flash?', '2006-05-08 22:34:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(2395124, 328195, 33145, '<td valign="top">Dude, shots like this show that your skill has no ceiling. You deserve every ribbon you''ve received recently as they are all stand-out shots. You continue to inspire. Well done.</td>', 'Dude, shots like this show that your skill has no ceiling. You deserve every ribbon you''ve received recently as they are all stand-out shots. You continue to inspire. Well done.', '2006-05-08 22:38:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(2395141, 327853, 40718, '<td valign="top">I was one of those 70 fives.  I think the biggest thing I saw that could be fixed is a color cast.  The shot appears to my eyes to be blue.<br/> <br/>The composition is nicely off center.  The distant background isn''t that great and doesn''t help the picture.  It also appears to be quite slanted which may have been done on purpose to compose the flower, but it''s another reason that background isn''t helping.</td>', 'I was one of those 70 fives.  I think the biggest thing I saw that could be fixed is a color cast.  The shot appears to my eyes to be blue. The composition is nicely off center.  The distant background isn''t that great and doesn''t help the picture.  It also appears to be quite slanted which may have been done on purpose to compose the flower, but it''s another reason that background isn''t helping.', '2006-05-08 22:48:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2395144, 328003, 30982, '<td valign="top">I''d say this is a darn bit better than the brown.  Very creative and indeed very humorous.  Well done and congrats on the high placement!</td>', 'I''d say this is a darn bit better than the brown.  Very creative and indeed very humorous.  Well done and congrats on the high placement!', '2006-05-08 22:49:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2395146, 328435, 40718, '<td valign="top">I liked the subject, but I didn''t like the setting.  It looks too snapshot.  By this I mean that it doesn''t look like much effort went into the background.  Could you have done this at a park or in some nicely urban alley?<br/> <br/>Another issue is the color cast.  It looks very blue, especially in the tones of the skater''s skin.  The picture could likely use more contrast as well.</td>', 'I liked the subject, but I didn''t like the setting.  It looks too snapshot.  By this I mean that it doesn''t look like much effort went into the background.  Could you have done this at a park or in some nicely urban alley? Another issue is the color cast.  It looks very blue, especially in the tones of the skater''s skin.  The picture could likely use more contrast as well.', '2006-05-08 22:50:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2395172, 327915, 38496, '<td valign="top">A beautiful girl always makes for a nice picture!  The skin tones came out really nicely in this.  The desat makes her ''pop'' from the background nicely.  I would have liked to see the drummers face maybe (stretching for ways to improve this Ü).  Overall this is a great shot.  Sounds like you had a really fun weekend!</td>', 'A beautiful girl always makes for a nice picture!  The skin tones came out really nicely in this.  The desat makes her ''pop'' from the background nicely.  I would have liked to see the drummers face maybe (stretching for ways to improve this Ü).  Overall this is a great shot.  Sounds like you had a really fun weekend!', '2006-05-08 23:03:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2395249, 328534, 52336, '<td valign="top">Overall, a very attractive image with excellent lighting, though the subject would not have suffered from being even more lit.  Technically, this is a good photo, with nice composition and interesting highlights.  I think though that it is banal; technically good photos must also have an interesting and engaging subject (and I know this because I''m the king of technically acceptable and otherwise meaningless photographs).  I really would have liked this to have done better, though, because I think it really deserves it.</td>', 'Overall, a very attractive image with excellent lighting, though the subject would not have suffered from being even more lit.  Technically, this is a good photo, with nice composition and interesting highlights.  I think though that it is banal; technically good photos must also have an interesting and engaging subject (and I know this because I''m the king of technically acceptable and otherwise meaningless photographs).  I really would have liked this to have done better, though, because I think it really deserves it.', '2006-05-08 23:28:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2395256, 327533, 55642, '<td valign="top">Hey there -<br/> <br/>This isn''t a bad idea, but cropping such a small area from such a large photo rarely works out for the better. The quality just isn''t there. Moreover, the light is rather harsh, so toning it down and adding some warmer tones helps a lot. Finally, the subject is just rather blah. DPC is kinda overloaded on so-so flower shots at the moment and the magenta bloom in the photo looks rather sickly. <br/> <br/>For what it''s worth, here''s my workshop. More than anything else I tried to just clean up the house fly. All my steps are listed there. FWIW, the demo version of Neat Image is a free download if you don''t already have it. <br/> <br/>[thumb]390689[/thumb]<br/> <br/>EDIT: The thumbnail button doesn''t seem to want to work here.. I''ll try posting it on your topic, and if it doesn''t like that either, then look in my portfolio under the Workshop folder. ;-)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-05-08 22:33:43.</i></td>', 'Hey there - This isn''t a bad idea, but cropping such a small area from such a large photo rarely works out for the better. The quality just isn''t there. Moreover, the light is rather harsh, so toning it down and adding some warmer tones helps a lot. Finally, the subject is just rather blah. DPC is kinda overloaded on so-so flower shots at the moment and the magenta bloom in the photo looks rather sickly.  For what it''s worth, here''s my workshop. More than anything else I tried to just clean up the house fly. All my steps are listed there. FWIW, the demo version of Neat Image is a free download if you don''t already have it.  [thumb]390689[/thumb] EDIT: The thumbnail button doesn''t seem to want to work here.. I''ll try posting it on your topic, and if it doesn''t like that either, then look in my portfolio under the Workshop folder. ;-)', '2006-05-08 23:31:54.000000', '2006-05-08 23:33:43.000000', 0),
(2395262, 327848, 52336, '<td valign="top">A little underexposed, and perhaps not technically excellent, and also somewhat prosaic subject matter for a free study.  I do like the placement of the road in the frame, and it''s otherwise put together nicely, but suffers from a bit of softness, and slightly blown highlights between the branches.  The image size itself should probably have taken advantage of the full 640.  Lovely colour.</td>', 'A little underexposed, and perhaps not technically excellent, and also somewhat prosaic subject matter for a free study.  I do like the placement of the road in the frame, and it''s otherwise put together nicely, but suffers from a bit of softness, and slightly blown highlights between the branches.  The image size itself should probably have taken advantage of the full 640.  Lovely colour.', '2006-05-08 23:35:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(2395298, 328487, 25397, '<td valign="top">You weren''t lying, this is great! :-D</td>', 'You weren''t lying, this is great! :-D', '2006-05-08 23:46:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(2395303, 328411, 52336, '<td valign="top">Lovely, lovely image, with soft shadows and interesting shapes that really stand out for me.  I love the contrasts in the textures between the vase-shape and column, steps, and sidewalk (?).  Colours are gentle, muted, and beautiful.  Everything is set off so well, and I really start to get curious about where the steps are leading, and where this is.  Composition really satisfies.  Beautiful, congratulations.</td>', 'Lovely, lovely image, with soft shadows and interesting shapes that really stand out for me.  I love the contrasts in the textures between the vase-shape and column, steps, and sidewalk (?).  Colours are gentle, muted, and beautiful.  Everything is set off so well, and I really start to get curious about where the steps are leading, and where this is.  Composition really satisfies.  Beautiful, congratulations.', '2006-05-08 23:48:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(2395307, 328015, 54540, '<td valign="top">Another great shot!  I''ve been an astronomy buff since the late ''70s - and this is a great shot considering the tough subject and tight field of view.<br/> <br/>Too bad about the DQ, but this just adds fuel to the reasons why we need a "Space ''n Stuff" challenge.  (It had to have DQ''d even before I could vote on it!  I do not recall seeing this in the set, and I voted 100%.)<br/> <br/>Advanced editing with a special rule allowing stacks.  For those without a scope - any image that conveys "Space" - thinking museums, satellite tracks, star trails, Iridium flares, etc...<br/> <br/>Keep up the great work!<br/>ralfw</td>', 'Another great shot!  I''ve been an astronomy buff since the late ''70s - and this is a great shot considering the tough subject and tight field of view. Too bad about the DQ, but this just adds fuel to the reasons why we need a "Space ''n Stuff" challenge.  (It had to have DQ''d even before I could vote on it!  I do not recall seeing this in the set, and I voted 100%.) Advanced editing with a special rule allowing stacks.  For those without a scope - any image that conveys "Space" - thinking museums, satellite tracks, star trails, Iridium flares, etc... Keep up the great work!ralfw', '2006-05-08 23:50:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2395394, 328147, 37893, '<td valign="top">Hey James. Ok from my first impression of this image during voting I gave it a 6 but couldn''t give it any more than that for the following reasons:<br/>- the colors needs a boost in contrast and saturation to make the blue really pop<br/>- the cut-off tail is a bit of a distraction<br/>- last and most importantly, for this image to really have the wow factor, the whale, a beluga it seems, should have been facing the camera so that eye contact is created between the viewer and the subject<br/> <br/>There are dark areas in the photo that is somewhat hard to comprehend and the weight of the image is gravitating towards the top as most of the activity is there.<br/> <br/>It''s not a bad finish though I expected it to be a bit higher than it placed. Shooting through thick glass is a hard task and nothing to take lightly. I think you''ve done well however, in a Free Study, impact is critical for high votes and comments.<br/> <br/>Good luck man.<br/> <br/>Cheers,<br/> <br/>Rikki</td>', 'Hey James. Ok from my first impression of this image during voting I gave it a 6 but couldn''t give it any more than that for the following reasons:- the colors needs a boost in contrast and saturation to make the blue really pop- the cut-off tail is a bit of a distraction- last and most importantly, for this image to really have the wow factor, the whale, a beluga it seems, should have been facing the camera so that eye contact is created between the viewer and the subject There are dark areas in the photo that is somewhat hard to comprehend and the weight of the image is gravitating towards the top as most of the activity is there. It''s not a bad finish though I expected it to be a bit higher than it placed. Shooting through thick glass is a hard task and nothing to take lightly. I think you''ve done well however, in a Free Study, impact is critical for high votes and comments. Good luck man. Cheers, Rikki', '2006-05-09 00:33:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(2395447, 328249, 37893, '<td valign="top">This is a great shot Marc. I think it''s just way to expansive though. The placement of the tree is spot on and the curve of the hills is right on the ROTs. I think what hurt this a bit is the fact that there is hardly any definition in the tree since it''s too small. The minimalist approach works well for me. However, seeing I am looking at this in front of a bright monitor and I can sense that the foreground is dark, leads me to believe that most will perceived a dark foreground :( Great eye though ;)</td>', 'This is a great shot Marc. I think it''s just way to expansive though. The placement of the tree is spot on and the curve of the hills is right on the ROTs. I think what hurt this a bit is the fact that there is hardly any definition in the tree since it''s too small. The minimalist approach works well for me. However, seeing I am looking at this in front of a bright monitor and I can sense that the foreground is dark, leads me to believe that most will perceived a dark foreground :( Great eye though ;)', '2006-05-09 00:55:23.000000', NULL, 0),
